{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And Abraham returned to his place.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): this is Elonei Mamre, for from there he had first set out." "<b>And it is plausible</b> to interpret 'to his place' as referring to his trait, which is the hosting of guests; for once he had fulfilled his obligation toward those guests with food and drink and escort, he would return to seek more guests. And this is 'he returned to his place' — for the soul of Abraham was drawn from the trait of חסד, and that trait was his place. And it is also possible to interpret 'to his place' as referring to the boundary of his physical sensations and the measure of his body: for as long as the Shekhinah was with him, he was entirely intellect, abstracted from all matters of matter, and his sensations were nullified; nothing remained standing before HaShem but form and soul — and that is the pure and luminous intellect. Once the Shekhinah withdrew, he returned to his sensations and to the limits of bodily measures, and this is 'and Abraham returned to his place' — that is, to the boundary of his body's measures, for a person's 'place' is that which encompasses and delimits him." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'And Abraham returned to his place' — the attribute of חסד returned to its place when it found no merit, and then the attribute of דין acts; this is what Scripture says immediately after: ״ויבאו המלאכים סדומה״, and it is written ״ויהי בשחת אלהים״. And the attribute of דין has no action until the attribute of חסד delivers them over in judgment, and then the attribute of דין acts upon those judged. And this is the secret of the verse (Genesis 22:6): ״ויקח בידו את האש ואת המאכלת״ — that is, that the attribute of חסד gathers the forces of יצחק and delivers them over in judgment, and this is ״וילכו שניהם יחדו״ — and יצחק walks after אברהם with his permission and by his agreement. And behold, the attribute of דין is bound before the attribute of חסד, for were it not so the world would be destroyed; and this is the secret of (ibid.) ״ויעקד את יצחק בנו״. And this is the plain meaning of the phrase 'ורב חסד' — that חסד is multiplied over דין, and this is clear."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:36.217757418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}